transformations list, sources_kept empty (since integration_source_ids empty), files array with path and content, notes.\n\nHypothesis: \"Replacing std::cin with a custom buffered fast integer scanner reduces input parsing overhead for the large N×N matrix, while preserving the OpenMP parallelization and SIMD reduction over submatrix sums; this should lower total runtime.\"\n\nTransformations: [\"Replace iostream-based input with a custom fread-backed FastScanner\", \"Keep existing OpenMP parallel-for and omp simd directives\"].\n\nBut we need to list transformations as strings. We'll include.\n\nLet's craft the code carefully, ensuring no syntax errors.\n\nPotential issue: The fast scanner's readInt template uses `T val = 0;` but for int, if number is negative, sign handling works. However, after reading digits, it consumes one non-digit char (whitespace) and discards it; that's fine because next call will skip whitespace anyway. But what about EOF? If c==0, the while loop exits, out set, but we've consumed EOF; subsequent reads will get 0 again and return false. That's okay.\n\nBut there is a subtle bug: In `readInt`, after reading digits, if c is not digit (e.g., whitespace), we don't store it back; that's fine because next call skips leading whitespace. However, if the input has no trailing whitespace and EOF occurs right after last digit, getChar returns 0, loop exits, out set, but then subsequent calls will see size==0 and return false. That's correct.\n\nAlso note: The scanner uses `char` for buffer; fread may read binary? Input is text, fine.\n\nLet's also include `<cstring>`? Not needed.\n\nNow write code:\n\n```cpp\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <climits>\n#include <cstdio>\n\nclass FastScanner {\n    static const int BUFSIZE = 1 << 20;\n    char buf[BUFSIZE];\n    int idx, size;\npublic:\n    FastScanner() : idx(0), size(0) {}\n    inline char getChar() {\n        if (idx >= size) {\n            size = fread(buf, 1, BUFSIZE, stdin);\n            idx = 0;\n            if (size == 0) return 0;\n        }\n        return buf[idx++];\n    }\n    template<typename T>\n    bool readInt(T& out) {\n        char c;\n        do { c = getChar(); } while (c <= ' ');\n        if (!c) return false;\n        int sign = 1;\n        if (c == '-') { sign = -1; c = getChar(); }\n        T val = 0;\n        while (c >= '0' && c <= '9') {\n            val = val * 10 + (c - '0');\n            c = getChar();\n        }\n        out = static_cast<T>(val * sign);\n        return true;\n    }\n};\n\nint main() {\n    FastScanner fs;\n    int n, s;\n    if (!fs.readInt(n) || !fs.readInt(s)) return 0;\n\n    const int W = n + 1;\n    std::vector<long long> pref((n + 1) * (n + 1), 0LL);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        long long row_sum = 0;\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            int x;\n            fs.readInt(x);\n            row_sum += x;\n            pref[(i + 1) * W + (j + 1)] = pref[i * W + (j + 1)] + row_sum;\n        }\n    }\n\n    long long mxSum = LLONG_MIN;\n    const int limit_i = n - s + 1;\n\n    #pragma omp parallel for reduction(max:mxSum) schedule(static)\n    for (int i = 0; i < limit_i; ++i) {\n        const long long* __restrict row_pref = &pref[i * W];\n        const long long* __restrict bottom_pref = &pref[(i + s) * W];\n        #pragma omp simd reduction(max:mxSum)\n        for (int j = 0; j < limit_i; ++j) {\n            long long sum = bottom_pref[j + s] - row_pref[j + s] - bottom_pref[j] + row_pref[j];\n            if (sum > mxSum) mxSum = sum;\n        }\n    }\n\n    std::cout << static_cast<int>(mxSum) << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n```\n\nThis is essentially same as before but with fast scanner.\n\nCould we also add `#pragma omp simd` with `aligned`? Not necessary.\n\nLet's consider if the fast scanner might be slower due to function call overhead per integer. We can inline readInt; it's already inline. The getChar is inline too. Should be fine.\n\nM